.TH "OPS\-RUN" 1 "" "ops" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ops\-run \- run a command on a host
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBops run\fR [flags] <host> [\-\-] <command...>
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fI<host>\fR
where to run it [edge|core]
.RS
.RS 2
\fBedge\fR \- the edge pool
.br
\fBcore\fR
.RE
.RE
.TP
\fI<command...>\fR
the command and its arguments (passed through as typed)
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fIstring\fR
how to print results (default text) [text|json|yaml]
.RS
.RS 2
\fBtext\fR \- aligned columns
.br
\fBjson\fR
.br
\fByaml\fR \- human\-friendly
.RE
.RE
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
print help
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
say more (repeatable)
.br
repeat to count: \-vvv
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fIstring\fR
when to color (default auto) [auto|always|never]
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBops\fR(1)
